  <!-- 04 Why we are building it (soft band): three "rather than" cards -->
  <section class="section" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-mark"><span class="numeral">04</span><p class="eyebrow">Why we are building it</p></div>
        <h2 id="why-title">The Right Starting Point, Made Personal.</h2>
        <p class="subcopy">Producers often invest in MIDI packs, loop libraries, DAW templates and AI generation tools simply to reach the right starting point. CuTTI is designed to make that starting point yours.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hgrid hgrid--3 hgrid--bottom lp-rather">
        <article class="practice">
          <p class="lp-rather__was">Rather than searching through another MIDI pack</p>
          <h3>Describe the Musical Idea.</h3>
          <p class="practice__body">Say what the song needs, in your words. CuTTI turns the direction into parts you can play, edit and replace.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="practice">
          <p class="lp-rather__was">Rather than adapting your song to another template</p>
          <h3>Start from Your Own Direction.</h3>
          <p class="practice__body">The arrangement structure is built around your brief: the sections, their order and the instruments in each one.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="practice">
          <p class="lp-rather__was">Rather than stopping at generated audio</p>
          <h3>Keep Producing in Your DAW.</h3>
          <p class="practice__body">The result is a Logic Pro project, not a rendered file. Every track, region and note stays open for the next decision.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 05 Ask it (dark band): conversational edits -->
  <section class="section band-dark" id="ask" aria-labelledby="ask-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-mark"><span class="numeral">05</span><p class="eyebrow">Conversational production</p></div>
        <h2 id="ask-title">Ask for the Change. Keep Producing.</h2>
        <p class="subcopy">Work with the session the way you would brief a session player. Each request becomes concrete edits in Logic Pro that you can keep, tweak or undo.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="lp-asks" role="list">
        <li class="lp-ask"><span class="lp-ask__caret" aria-hidden="true">›</span>Build an arrangement.</li>
